Batching regression audit and fix

Baseline inspected: 5dc3d3c:harness/src/sender.cpp
Regression found before this pass: harness/src/sender.cpp had removed the sender Batch helper, --batch-size, --batch-timeout-us, and sendmmsg batching. It used direct_send with one send() per datagram.
Fix applied in this pass: restored --batch-size default 32 and --batch-timeout-us default 50, restored sendmmsg batching, and routed raw data frames plus FEC parity/data datagrams through the same batcher.

Current code evidence
- harness/src/sender.cpp:40 batch_size default 32
- harness/src/sender.cpp:41 batch_timeout_us default 50
- harness/src/sender.cpp:124 parses --batch-size
- harness/src/sender.cpp:125 parses --batch-timeout-us
- harness/src/sender.cpp:216 calls sendmmsg
- harness/src/sender.cpp:225 increments sendmmsg_calls
- harness/src/sender.cpp:429 prints sendmmsg_calls, send_calls, max_sendmmsg_batch

Throughput probe setup
- WSL2 loopback, current repo, 700000 producer messages at 700000 msg/s, 65536 slots, receiver present, no benchmark/results writes.
- Throughput below is requested_count / sender wall time. Sender sent count is also reported because WSL saturation/lapping means the sender may not read all 700000 frames.

